# Red Hat Lightspeed terminology

Red Hat consolidated AI-powered services under the **Lightspeed** brand. Use current product names in **new** prose, UI copy, tooltips, card bodies, and marketing text on the site and in guides.

## Current names (use in new writing)

| Old name | Current name |
|----------|----------------|
| Ansible Lightspeed Code Assistant, Ansible Lightspeed (playbook generation) | **Automation code assistant** |
| Ansible Lightspeed Intelligent Assistant | **Automation intelligent assistant** |
| Red Hat Insights (console.redhat.com advisory/CVE context) | **Red Hat Lightspeed** |

**Capitalization:** Write **Automation code assistant** and **Automation intelligent assistant** with only the first letter of **Automation** capitalized. Do not use title case (`Automation Code Assistant`) unless quoting an external document literally.

## Red Hat Lightspeed remediations vs Automation code assistant

Two different capabilities often get conflated in AIOps copy:

| Capability | What it is | Wording in new prose |
|------------|------------|----------------------|
| **Red Hat Lightspeed** (console.redhat.com) | CVE, Advisor, Vulnerability, Inventory, **Remediations** -- Ansible content curated and maintained by Red Hat from errata, security data, and support expertise | **Publishes**, **provides**, or **curated / Red Hat-approved remediation playbooks**. Do **not** say Red Hat Lightspeed **generates** playbooks with AI or lump it with LLM codegen. |
| **Automation code assistant** | LLM-assisted playbook **authoring** in the IDE (formerly Ansible Lightspeed code assistant) | **Drafts** or **authoring-time** generation; humans review before promotion into AAP. |

**Automation intelligent assistant** is a third product (in-product admin help) -- not CVE remediations and not playbook codegen.

## When legacy names are OK

Keep old names when they match **existing** artifacts readers will see:

- Code, YAML, API paths, tokens, collection names, and variable names (e.g. `lightspeed_prompt`, `lightspeed_wca_token`)
- Job template, workflow, or project names in screenshots or examples
- Historical quotes, KB titles, or access.redhat.com links that have not been renamed

## Solution guides that discuss Lightspeed

Guides that explain AIOps or playbook generation should include the standard terminology blockquote once (early in the guide), matching `README-AIOps.md`:

> **Terminology update -- Lightspeed rebranding.**
>
> Red Hat has consolidated its AI-powered services under the **Lightspeed** brand. **Ansible Lightspeed Code Assistant** is now **Automation code assistant** (supports Gemini, Red Hat AI, or IBM watsonx). **Ansible Lightspeed Intelligent Assistant** is now **Automation intelligent assistant**. **Red Hat Insights** (console.redhat.com) is now **Red Hat Lightspeed**. The functionality is the same -- only the branding has changed. This guide uses both old and new names where they appear in existing code and screenshots.

## Common mistakes

- Bad (catalog/hero): "Ansible Lightspeed to generate remediation playbooks"
- Good: "Automation code assistant to generate remediation playbooks" (authoring) or "Red Hat Lightspeed curated remediations" (console.redhat.com)
- Bad: "generated by Red Hat Lightspeed" (implies AI)
- Good: "Red Hat-curated remediation playbooks from Red Hat Lightspeed"
